course: dictionary
lesson: 11212
title: Wonderland, a place that feels like a dream
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A wonderland is a place full of wonderful, magical or beautiful things. As a noun it can be one wonderland or two wonderlands. With a capital W, Wonderland is a name: the strange dream world Alice falls into in Lewis Carroll's book.
explain: The words around the word give you clues. «Alice's Adventures in Wonderland» is the name of a book, so the capital W tells you it is a name. In «a winter wonderland», there is no capital, and the clue is winter: everything is covered in snow, so the place is very beautiful at that time.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. In the story, Wonderland is a place where nothing follows normal rules: drinks make you shrink, and a cat grins and vanishes. Wonderland is strange and magical, but it is not always kind, because the Queen wants to cut off everyone's head.
fact: Wonderland means a place full of wonderful, magical or beautiful things.
fact: Wonderland with a capital W is the dream world in Lewis Carroll's book about Alice, published in 1865.
fact: In «a winter wonderland», the word describes a place that looks beautiful at a certain time, such as when everything is covered in snow.
fact: At the end of Alice, Alice wakes up, and it was a dream.
fact: In everyday talk, people call a place a wonderland when it seems too good or strange to be real.
exercise: «Alice's Adventures in Wonderland» is a book you can read twice. In this title, what is Wonderland? | A town in the north of England | A kind of winter snow | *A dream world from a famous book | A school for Victorian children
exercise: In «a winter wonderland», what does wonderland mean? | *A place that is very beautiful at a certain time | A school for young children | A place where nothing follows normal rules | A dark cave full of bats
exercise: In Wonderland, drinks make you shrink and a cat grins and vanishes. What is strange about Wonderland? | It is always cold and dark | Everything is exactly like home | *Nothing follows normal rules | It has no animals at all
test: In the story, Alice falls into Wonderland. Where does she go down? | Through an open window | Across a frozen lake | Up a tall mountain | *Down a rabbit hole
test: «The Queen wants to cut off everyone's head.» What does this tell you about Wonderland? | It is a place full of snow | It is a quiet school | *It is not always a gentle place | Everyone in it is very polite
exam: Mia says a wonderland is always a happy place. Who is right? | *No, a wonderland is any place full of wonderful, magical or beautiful things, and Wonderland can be strange and scary | Yes, a wonderland is always happy and safe | Yes, because every wonderland has snow | No, wonderlands are only found in books
